{"name":"Matt Black","hex":"#151515","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"matt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of matte."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of matte (“background, often painted or created with computers”).","Alternative spelling of mat (“an alloy in coppersmithing”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/matt"},{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"}],"entries":[{"title":"Matt Black (DJ)","blocks":[{"text":"Matthew Cohn, known by the stage name Matt Black, is a British DJ and one half of music duo Coldcut, who founded the Ninja Tune record label."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Matt_Black_-_Coldcut_%28Vienna_2006%29.jpg/330px-Matt_Black_-_Coldcut_%28Vienna_2006%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matt_Black_(DJ)","wikidata":"Q6788357"},{"title":"Matt Black (Canadian football)","blocks":[{"text":"Matthew Black is a Canadian former professional football defensive back who played ten seasons with the Toronto Argonauts of the Canadian Football League (CFL). He won two Grey Cup championships in 2012 and 2017."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/2023%2C_Alum39%2C_Matt_Black.jpg/330px-2023%2C_Alum39%2C_Matt_Black.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matt_Black_(Canadian_football)","wikidata":"Q6788360"},{"title":"Matt Black (photographer)","blocks":[{"text":"Matt Black is an American documentary photographer whose work has 